==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Power Driller Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Neo Driller Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Driller Cat is a high-risk, high-reward unit. He has fantastic range for a Super Rare Cat, and with a 90% weaken, even the likes of [[Master A.]], [[R.Ost]] and [[H. Nah]] will become almost harmless! The drawbacks are his blind spot, single target and low survivability - he can't be used against hordes, and if a threat that isn't weakened gets in his blind spot, it's safe to assume that whatever he was trying to hit will immediately escape his clutches and move forward. Driller Cat is stackable, but his long recharge time (71.2 seconds) and his tendency to easily move forward can make doing so difficult.

[[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floors 30]] and [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 40|40]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]] are some of his most valuable applications, but being a CC unit, he's useless outside of his niche.

==='''True Form'''===
The most notable gain of Driller Cat's True Form is an increased attack rate, massively increasing his uptime and rendering it permanent with enough Weaken combos. The Strong ability is unlikely to ever come into play, as Driller still doesn't have remarkable DPS or health against the Traitless enemies you're trying to Weaken, though he can take advantage of his Knockbacks against a weakened enemy; while much better against Traitless than before, he still bears all the same core flaws.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Sniper}}

