==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 11.2 Update|Version 11.2]], Driller Cat, [[Piledriver Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Piledriver Cat]], [[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cutter Cat]], [[Backhoe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Backhoe Cat]] and [[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Miter Saw Cat]] could only be unlocked when "Grandon Mining Corps" was part of the current pool.
*In his Japanese description, Power Driller Cat is stated to be drilling for Tokunaga reserves. The [https://enacademic.com/dic.nsf/enwiki/9101250 Tokunaga] were claimed descendants of another clan, Fujiwara, which ruled until Edo period.
*Driller Cat could be seen in [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Guardians]]' attack animation before he was added to the game, albeit with a darker color scheme, the number "01" instead of "06", and the mustachioed "captain cat" present in most of the [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] units as the pilot.
**In the Ultra Form, [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Saviours]], a conceptual Ultra Form design for Driller Cat, along with all other Grandon Mining Corps units can be seen during its attack animation. They have the same color scheme of all other [[Frontline Assault IRON LEGION (Gacha Event)|IRON LEGION]] Ultra Forms, that being red and black with gold lining.
*In The Battle Cats Unite!, Driller Cat was changed to target all enemies, but in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Update History#Patch 1.0.6 (July 14, 2023)|Patch 1.0.6]], this was no longer the case since Driller Cat could not target [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]].
**This unique phenomenon in enemy targeting is shared with Gato Amigo and Pastry Cat, however, those True Forms are not obtainable without save file editing, which leaves Driller Cat the only unit to see this unique visual.
**Interestingly enough, looking into the character's internal stats, it did receive the check to target Zombies, but for some reason is not active in the game itself.

